  "review_text": "Independent substantive review by review-palette-651-20261003 of PR671 exact head bd48350a9fed47b6ca66401a0a21db4ca8cee4ba against base 277b8ecbb3199ae3d5fb07bab96353d17a049b1c: accepted as the second bounded, partial #529 contribution. This is not full issue acceptance or permission to run migrations or publish.\n\nI inspected the additive SQL guards, complete version3 contract/export/restore, private GET routing, actual SQLite/PostgreSQL tests, documentation, all63 changed-file byte receipts and retained attempts. Both SQL implementations now agree with the merged pure status/source/null branches. Exact replay keeps original raw provenance; the two retirement uniqueness keys are checked before either conflict-ignore form can silently discard a different retained identity/source/reason/metadata. The independent initial findings, original collision proof and corrected reassessment are preserved verbatim. I independently reran all41 focused controls on this exact committed source:41 passed,0 failures,0 skips. The separately reproduced complete catalog hashes match unchanged final SQL/contract/test bytes.\n\nThe version3 path covers all26 factual tables and fails on uninstalled/altered schema, missing guards, unknown tables or changed source pins. Actual restore controls cover all populated collections, raw JSON whitespace/zero/false/null, retained corrections, ordered identity hashes, deferred-FK rollback, enabled guards and sequence. Owner/empty-target acknowledgements, maintenance read-only capture, cursor/version binding and bounded transport are retained. These SQL backups preserve media registrations, not object-store payload bytes. All27 legacy source pins match original baseline, incorporated current main and reviewed head. The original whole journal is retained and precisely one entry appended; no legacy migration/snapshot, v1/v2 contract or research/factual path is rewritten.\n\nI inspected the actual source-bound625-pass full regression,41-pass focused and9-pass staging/transport receipts, successful hosted archive reserve audit (262522880 uncompressed bytes, zero violations), and older failed/superseded runs. I did not independently rerun the full regression or hosted build. Native workerd D1 failed in unchanged0008 with too many terms in compound SELECT, before0010; its log/hash and explicit unavailable status are honest. Local SQLite/PGlite evidence is not a native D1 pass. Legacy D10000-0007 must not advertise typed capabilities, and native forward compatibility requires reviewed follow-up if needed.\n\nRetirement/replacement integrity is guaranteed for the supported atomic ingestion-plus-journal batch, not arbitrary standalone owner SQL. Typed module/metric/metadata/source/registry/regional approval checks belong to the unfinished controlled adapter. One final budgeted PR remains for import/read/capabilities, static/prepared/snapshot parity, labeled v2-compatible projection and closed owner forward-workflow/role integration; domain children stay blocked. This PR honestly uses only Refs #529. If that final scope cannot fit, obtain coordinator-reviewed follow-ups rather than a fourth PR.\n\nCanonical ownership currently matches author/branch/claim9ea71518 with live_work=false; required exact-head CI and serialized queue/actual merge verification remain separate gates. No provider operation, Site publication, geographic/historical approval, physical-device certificate, token access or formal mandatory manifest binding is conferred by this review. New commits invalidate this head-bound acceptance.",
